.SS Now Playing Widget
The right side of the status line shows the currently playing track, via
.IR ~/.tmux/scripts/now-playing.sh .
It checks playerctl (Linux), then nowplaying-cli, then Spotify and Chrome
music tabs via AppleScript.
.TP
.B Click
Focus the app that is playing (Spotify, or the Chrome tab on a music site)
.PP
The click is wired up with a
.B range=user|player
marker in the status-right format and a
.B MouseDown1Status
binding in
.IR ~/.tmux.conf .
Note that user ranges fire the plain
.B Status
mouse key, not
.BR StatusRight .
.SH GHOSTTY
.SS Clicking Links with tmux Mouse Mode
When tmux mouse mode is enabled, use modifier keys to bypass tmux and click links:
.TP
.B Cmd+Click
Open link (macOS)
.TP
.B Shift+Cmd+Click
Open link (alternative)
.SH SSH
.SS macOS Keychain Integration
SSH keys are automatically unlocked via macOS Keychain. Configuration in
.IR ~/.ssh/config :
.PP
.RS
.nf
Host *
    AddKeysToAgent yes
    UseKeychain yes
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.fi
.RE
.SS Adding Keys
Use the macOS built-in ssh-add (not Homebrew's) to store passphrases in Keychain:
.PP
.RS
.B /usr/bin/ssh-add --apple-use-keychain ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.RE
.PP
Keys are loaded automatically when first needed.
