.SH HOMEBREW
Packages are managed via a global Brewfile at
.IR ~/.Brewfile .
.SS Installing Packages
.TP
.B brew bundle add --global brew <package>
Install a package and add it to the global Brewfile
.TP
.B brew bundle --global
Install everything in the Brewfile
.SS Upgrading
.TP
.B brew upgrade
Upgrade all installed packages to latest versions
.SS Cleanup
.TP
.B brew bundle --global cleanup
Remove packages not listed in the Brewfile
.TP
.B brew bundle --global cleanup --force
Actually uninstall them (without --force it's a dry run)
.SH MACOS DESKTOP
.SS Raycast
.TP
.B ⌥ Space
Launch Raycast (Option+Space)
.SS Ice
Manages the macOS menu bar icons so they don't run into the notch. Hides, shows, and rearranges status bar items.
.SS Asimov
Runs as a Homebrew background service and excludes dependency directories
.RI ( node_modules ,
.IR .venv ,
.IR target ,
.IR DerivedData ,
and ~30 other patterns) from Time Machine backups. A directory is only excluded when its sentinel config file sits alongside it, so
.I node_modules
is skipped only next to a
.IR package.json .
The yadm bootstrap starts the service; it then runs once a day on its own.
.TP
.B asimov --dry-run --stats
Preview what would be excluded, with sizes. Changes nothing
.TP
.B asimov
Apply the exclusions now
.TP
.B brew services list
Check that the asimov service is running
.SH CLAUDE CODE AND CODEX
.SS Shared Commands
The command instructions in
.I ~/.claude/commands/
are the single source of truth for
.BR pry ,
.BR recon ,
.BR reviewy ,
.BR eli-review ,
and
.BR fix-merge-conflicts .
Claude Code runs them as
.BR /pry ,
.BR /recon ,
.BR /reviewy ,
.BR /eli-review ,
and
.BR /fix-merge-conflicts .
The matching Codex skills in
.I ~/.codex/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
read those same command files and pass along any arguments. In Codex, invoke
them as
.B $pry
(and similarly for the other names), or select one through
.BR /skills .
.PP
The files in
.I ~/.codex/prompts/
also provide legacy
.B /prompts:<name>
aliases where custom prompts are supported. Custom prompts are deprecated;
the installed Codex CLI may not list these aliases. Use the skills above for
reliable invocation.
.SS Background Review Queues
Two launchd jobs poll GitHub every 5 minutes and start an agent only when
there is new work. The polling itself is plain
.B gh
and costs no tokens. Both jobs default to
.B codeclimate/edp
checked out at
.IR ~/Code/edp ,
and accept
.B [owner/repo] [checkout_dir]
to point them elsewhere.
.PP
Each job runs as a window in the dedicated tmux session
.BR agents ,
created through
.BR agents-window .
Windows are tagged with the
.B @job
option and get
.B $AGENT_JOB
in their environment. The usual click-to-focus notifications from
.I ~/.claude/hooks/notify.sh
and
.I ~/.codex/hooks/notify.sh
land in them like any other pane, so
.B tmux switch-client -t agents
(or a click on the notification) is how to pop in.
.TP
.B codex-review-queue
Reviews PRs that request my review directly (not through a team), skipping
drafts. All new PRs go into one
.B codex exec --approve-for-me \(dq$eli-review <urls>\(dq
run in window
.BR eli-review ,
with approvals handled by the auto reviewer. The window closes when the run
exits, and no new run starts while one is open. A run is killed after 45
minutes. A PR head commit is marked reviewed only when a run exits cleanly,
and gets at most 2 attempts, so a failing review doesn't retry every tick.
New commits queue the PR again. Failures are logged. Reviews post under my
account.
.TP
.B claude-reviewy-queue
Addresses review feedback on my own open PRs. When a PR has unanswered
threads (unresolved, and the last comment isn't mine), it starts an interactive
.B claude \(dq/loop 10m /reviewy <url> until ...\(dq
in window
.B reviewy-<pr>
on a worktree of the PR branch. A clean worktree that already has the branch
checked out is reused; if that worktree has uncommitted changes, the PR is
skipped (local
.B .env*
edits don't count). Each loop iteration addresses new threads from any
reviewer, rebases on main before every push, re-requests Copilot and fixes CI
failures the PR caused. The loop stops itself once Copilot's latest review is
on the head commit with nothing unresolved and every check passes, or asks me
if CI keeps failing or Copilot keeps finding things (rules in
.IR ~/.claude/commands/reviewy.md ).
Each set of unanswered comments is attempted once; a new
comment queues the PR again. Interactive Claude never exits on its own, so each run also closes
reviewy windows that are finished: Claude is idle at the prompt and the
window has had no activity for 30 minutes. Windows waiting on a permission
or a question are left open. Any other window running for over 6 hours is
closed as not converging; a new comment starts it again. Worktrees the job created are removed with the
window if they are clean.
.PP
.I ~/.claude/hooks/needs-you.sh
records what each Claude job is waiting on (a permission, an
.B AskUserQuestion
prompt, or idle at the prompt) in
.IR ~/.local/state/needs-you/<job> .
Every
.B gh
and network
.B git
call in the queues times out after 60 seconds, so a hung request can't stall
a queue.
The SwiftBar menu bar item
.RI ( ~/.config/swiftbar/needs-you.10s.sh )
lists the
.B agents
windows as working, \[u2691] waiting on me, or \[u2713] finished, and shows
\[u2691] N in the bar when any are waiting. Click one to attach in Ghostty.
.PP
Setup, with
.B agent-queues
(each command takes optional job names; the default is both):
.PP
.EX
# One-time: install SwiftBar and point it at ~/.config/swiftbar.
agent-queues setup

# See what each job would start right now. Nothing is written or started.
agent-queues preview

# Optional: mark everything currently pending as handled, so only new
# review requests / new feedback start an agent.
agent-queues seed

# Load the launchd jobs (poll every 5 min) and run them once now.
agent-queues on

# Loaded or not, last log lines, and running windows in "agents".
agent-queues status

# Unload. Windows already running in "agents" are left alone.
agent-queues off

# Any of these take job names, e.g. just the reviewy queue:
agent-queues on claude-reviewy-queue
.EE
.PP
Logs go to
.IR ~/Library/Logs/<job>.log .
List running jobs with
.B agents-window --list
and close one with
.BR "tmux kill-window -t agents:<job>" .
.SH SCRIPTS
Personal scripts live in
.I ~/.local/bin
and are on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B agent-queues setup|preview|seed|on|off|status [job...]
Set up and manage
.B codex-review-queue
and
.BR claude-reviewy-queue .
See
.BR "Background Review Queues" .
.TP
.B agents-window <job> <dir> <command...> | --has <job> | --list
Run a command as window
.B <job>
in the tmux session
.BR agents ,
unless that job is already running. See
.BR "Background Review Queues" .
.TP
.B claude-reviewy-queue [--dry-run | --seed] [owner/repo] [checkout_dir]
Run
.B /reviewy
in a tmux window for each of my PRs with changed review threads. See
.BR "Background Review Queues" .
.TP
.B codex-review-queue [--dry-run | --seed] [owner/repo] [checkout_dir]
Run Codex
.B $eli-review
on PRs requesting my review. See
.BR "Background Review Queues" .
.TP
.B gh-pr-review-context [<pr> | <owner> <repo> <pr>]
Print what a PR review needs in one call: metadata, description, unresolved
review threads, a local checkout (via
.BR gh-pr-worktree ),
and the
.B git diff
from that checkout annotated with the line numbers the GitHub review API
accepts. Used by
.BR /eli-review .
.TP
.B gh-pr-worktree <owner> <repo> <pr> | --cleanup <path>
Check out a PR's head commit for review. Reuses the current checkout or any
worktree already at that commit; otherwise adds a detached worktree (or, outside
the repo, a temporary clone) under
.IR $TMPDIR/eli-review .
Prints the path and the
.B --cleanup
command that removes it, plus the merge-base with the PR's base branch. Used by
.BR gh-pr-review-context .
.TP
.B gh-submit-review <owner> <repo> <pr> <review.json> [--dry-run]
Post a whole review (verdict, body, line comments) in one atomic call, pinned
to the PR head, with a footer saying an AI agent wrote it. A self-review is
downgraded to COMMENT. Run with
.B --help
for the JSON format.
.TP
.B fix-video-audio <input> [output]
Fix screen recordings (e.g. BetterCapture) that play silently in QuickTime. They often have several audio tracks, and QuickTime only plays the first one, which is usually silent system audio. The script drops silent tracks and keeps the audible one without re-encoding. If more than one track is audible, it mixes them into one. Output defaults to
.IR <input>_fixed.<ext> .
